CM ============================================================
CM 2-Element Endfire Phased Array — 20M (14.175 MHz)
CM TM-HYB-001 Rev A
CM
CM Two half-wave dipoles separated by λ/4 (5.29 m)
CM Element 1: 0°, Element 2: −90° (quadrature hybrid feed)
CM Height: 10 m above average ground (σ=0.005, εr=13)
CM
CM Expected pattern: unidirectional cardioid (endfire)
CM Front-to-back ratio: ≈10–12 dB theoretical
CM Gain: ≈5.2 dBd over single dipole
CM
CM Feed network: 90° quadrature hybrid coupler (TM-HYB-001)
CM  Port 1 (input): RF source, 50Ω
CM  Port 2 (0° out): Element 1 via λ/2 50Ω coax
CM  Port 3 (−90° out): Element 2 via λ/2 50Ω coax
CM
CM Coordinate system:
CM  X-axis: element separation direction
CM  Y-axis: along elements (wire axis)
CM  Z-axis: height above ground
CM
CM Endfire direction: +X axis
CM ============================================================
CE

CM === ELEMENT 1 (0°, at x=0) ===
CM Half-wave dipole: length = 0.495 × λ = 0.495 × 21.145m = 10.47m
CM Wire: 2mm diameter copper (#14 AWG equivalent)

GW 1 21 0.000 -5.235 10.000 0.000 5.235 10.000 0.001
CM  Tag=1, Segs=21, x1=0,y1=-5.235,z1=10m, x2=0,y2=+5.235,z2=10m, rad=1mm

CM === ELEMENT 2 (−90°, at x=λ/4=5.29m) ===
GW 2 21 5.292 -5.235 10.000 5.292 5.235 10.000 0.001
CM  Tag=2, Segs=21, λ/4 spacing = c/(4×14.175e6) = 5.292 m

CM === GROUND: Average (σ=0.005 S/m, εr=13) ===
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0 13.0 0.005

