CM Azimuth sweep at elevation 20° (typical low-angle DX)
RP 0 1 361 1000 20.0 0.0 1.0 1.0

CM Elevation sweep in endfire direction (phi=0°)
RP 0 91 1 1000 0.0 0.0 1.0 1.0

EN

CM ============================================================
CM EXPECTED RESULTS:
CM   Gain (endfire, 20° el): approximately 7.5 dBi (≈5.5 dBd)
CM   F/B ratio:              ≈10 dB
CM   Main lobe azimuth:      0° (endfire, +X direction)
CM   Feed impedance element 1: ≈ 50-j25 Ω (mutual coupling)
CM   Feed impedance element 2: ≈ 50-j25 Ω
CM
CM MUTUAL COUPLING NOTE:
CM   λ/4 spacing causes significant mutual coupling.
CM   Feed impedance ≠ free-space dipole (73Ω).
CM   Use current-forcing feed method OR add matching network.
CM   Quadrature hybrid provides inherent port isolation which
CM   forces equal currents regardless of element impedance variation.
